From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:55:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] UefiPayloadPkg: Reclaim the variable store through coreboot
 while locked

While coreboot keeps its option lock or MOR lock armed, the fault
tolerant write cannot reclaim the variable store: the locks refuse its
writes past the store and the erase of the store. Until the next boot
every write appends a record, and a full store fails the writes of the
OS; at runtime the variable driver without SMM never reclaims, since the
fault tolerant write is a boot service.

Add EDKII_PLATFORM_VARIABLE_RECLAIM_PROTOCOL, which the variable driver
without SMM tries before its fault tolerant write in FtwVariableSpace(),
and which lets it reclaim at runtime as well. SmmStoreFvbRuntimeDxe
installs it: with coreboot's SMMSTORE_CMD_RECLAIM available (a lock
armed), it writes the reclaimed store with the firmware volume header
into the staging area before the last block of the region and asks
coreboot to commit it, which checks the image whole before it replaces
the store. Otherwise it answers EFI_UNSUPPORTED and the fault tolerant
write reclaims as before; at runtime the write then fails as before.
